### Sensory Groove V2 - API de accesos
### Compatible con la extension "REST Client" de VS Code y con JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Ejecuta las peticiones en orden: las variables se encadenan solas.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@adminToken = sensory-admin-dev


### 0. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### 1. Subir comprobante (multipart/form-data)
# Ajusta la ruta del archivo al comprobante que quieras probar.
# @name crearTransferencia
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfer
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SensoryGrooveBoundary

--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="nombre"

Emiliano Vargas
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="whatsapp"

6142550381
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="accesos"

2
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comprobante"; filename="comprobante.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ../refs/WhatsApp Image 2026-08-19 at 12.53.38 PM(1).jpeg
--SensoryGrooveBoundary--


### Captura el id devuelto arriba
@transferId = {{crearTransferencia.response.body.id}}


### 2. Listado de pendientes SIN token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/transfers


### 3. Listado de pendientes CON token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/transfers
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}


### 4. Revisar el comprobante subido
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/transfers/{{transferId}}/comprobante
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}


### 5. Escanear ANTES de aprobar -> "Acceso no válido o no aprobado"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SG-2026-{{transferId}}"
}


### 6. Aprobar la transferencia (imprime el envio simulado de WhatsApp)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

{
  "id": "{{transferId}}",
  "action": "approve"
}


### 7. Re-resolver la misma transferencia -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

{
  "id": "{{transferId}}",
  "action": "reject"
}


### 8. Descargar el QR generado
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/transfers/{{transferId}}/qr
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}


### 9. Escanear el acceso aprobado -> "Acceso Válido"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SG-2026-{{transferId}}"
}


### 10. Re-escanear -> warning "Acceso ya escaneado"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "{{transferId}}"
}


### 11. QR malformado -> "QR Invalido"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/scan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "no-soy-un-qr"
}


### 12. Rechazar una transferencia
# @name crearRechazo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfer
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SensoryGrooveBoundary

--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="nombre"

Prueba Rechazo
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="whatsapp"

6142854941
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="accesos"

1
--SensoryGrooveBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comprobante"; filename="comprobante.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ../refs/WhatsApp Image 2026-08-19 at 12.53.38 PM(1).jpeg
--SensoryGrooveBoundary--


###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

{
  "id": "{{crearRechazo.response.body.id}}",
  "action": "reject"
}
